rts byte-equality between two independently-saved reconciler stores. The saved JSON embeds created_at/updated_at wall-clock timestamps, so when the two save() calls straddle a 1-second boundary the bytes differ (observed on Gerrit change 2209 CI, ubuntu-latest py3.13: 'At index 72 diff: 4 != 3', created_at 06:04:43Z vs 06:04:44Z). Passed on py3.11/py3.12/macos-3.13 in the same run. Root cause: wall-clock dependency the check_wall_clock_asserts gate did not catch. Fix: freeze/inject a fixed clock across both stores' saves so timestamps are deterministic. Discovered while landing olm (MCP client configs); unrelated to that change.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c49a-225d-2bc0-4478","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky wall-clock race in test_rich_reemit_state byte-equivalence test","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["264ecc87-f2d5-4368-9d57-b17616e79493","b3f64eba-faee-4131-b630-a353638345f2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787649978007588001,"uuid":"009aa59a-dc53-4805-be29-28f7ca1336b4"}